.TITLE "clear"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Clears the terminal screen. it is used to __remove clutter__ and reset the visual state of your terminal window for a clean workspace.

.DIV "TLDR"
**clear**
Clears all previous output from the terminal display.
> 

**clear -x**
Clears the screen but preserves the scrollback buffer on some terminals.
> __-x__ exclude scrollback flag

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Using __clear__ does not delete your command history; it simply scrolls the visible area down or resets the display. Many users prefer the keyboard shortcut __Ctrl+L__ as a faster alternative to typing the command.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"


documentation: __https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man1/clear.1.html__
